diff --git a/Samples~/SongReactiveLandscape/README.md b/Samples~/SongReactiveLandscape/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3d6566fa746aac6e867eca9ca85229acb92a1e7f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Samples~/SongReactiveLandscape/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Song-reactive landscape (Phase 3B sample)
+
+**Runtime sample for Unity 6 + URP.** This sample generates every tree, grass blade,
+rolling hill, star quad and warp sculpture in code; it imports no models or
+textures, and includes **no song audio or presumed song matches**.
+
+## One-click scene creation
+
+1. Install the DanceFlow.Unity package and import the **Song Reactive Landscape**
+   sample through Package Manager > Samples. Assign a URP pipeline asset.
+2. Choose **Tools > DanceFlow > Samples > Create Synthetic Motion Landscape**.
+   Alternative menu entries generate *Arcadians*, *The Truth is a Virus*, and
+   *Star Lights Glow (Mystery Liquid Kick)* branded scenes with independent metadata.
+3. Press Play. This first run is explicitly **SYNTHETIC PREVIEW**, with generated
+   preview curves following the Phase 1 beat clock. Look for the on-screen label.
+4. In the scene's `SongShowcaseBootstrap`, assign a locally imported `AudioClip`
+   to the accompanying `AudioSource`. For Star Lights Glow set the correct BPM
+   **for that exact mix** in `reviewedSongBpm`. No BPM or beat phase is guessed.
+5. Import a canonical `dancerudiments.recording` JSON using **Assets > DanceFlow
+   > Import DanceRudiments Recording JSON...**.
+6. Assign its `MotionRecordingAsset` to `MotionSignalBus`, switch its Source to
+   **Imported Recording**, select four source channels, and explicitly acknowledge
+   the **same original source timeline** or configure master-beat retiming.
+   The recording contains no implicit proof of association with the song.
+7. For the optional full GPU sample buffer, enable it on the scene's
+   `MotionRecordingGpuBridge`. It uses the bus's already-validated recording pip;
+   there is no second, independently configured clock. On unsupported GPUs or recordings >1,048,576 scalar samples the
+   CPU-fed four channel globals continue working.
+
+The four shader slots default to **x / y / z / x** for the native catalogue's
+three-axis recordings. For 4-band StemLab recordings, replace them with
+`band_000`...`band_003`. For any arbitrary N-dimensional recording the names
+must match the imported JSON exactly. A channel that doesn't exist contributes
+zero rather than silently being substituted by unrelated audio.
+
+## Effects
+
+- `ProceduralLandscape` generates ~3,000 grass blades as one mesh, 14 trees,
+  a procedural ground mesh, star quads, and a warping helix.
+- `MotionSignalBus`: four synchronised float64 sampled channels (float32 shader
+  uniforms) with source-accurate pip mapping; synthetic preview remains distinct.
+- `MotionLandscape.shader`: gust-driven grass and canopy sway, trunk bending,
+  radial ground ripples, RGB palette rotation and helix torsion/expansion. `RecordedMotionWarp.shader` additionally samples
+  the actual optional float32 GPU recording buffer (channels 0/1) when enabled,
+  otherwise uses the live CPU-sampled motion uniforms.
+- `SongShowcaseAtmosphere`: modulates fog, sky colour and directional light;
+  restores previous settings when disabled.
+- `MotionPropertyDriver`: optional typed Light, ParticleSystem and Renderer
+  property bindings; also works with other shaders. Configure in the Inspector.
+- `MotionRecordingGpuBridge`: optional bounded StructuredBuffer with full
+  native-sample values converted to float32 for HLSL sampling. Only one master
+  song can own the global buffer; no per-song instancing yet.
+
+## Song reference notes
+
+The `song-sources.json` manifest documents four independently configured song
+entries. StemLab's Arcadians benchmark reports `groove_b_played`,
+`groove_b_grid` and `lfo_morph` among its leading *comparative* native pattern
+matches. Match scores are not confidence probabilities or proof of alignment.
+The file does **not** bundle the Arcadians report or sampled motion tables.
+
+The two **Star Lights Glow** mixes are treated separately: *Mystery Liquid Kick*
+and *Anthem*. No source BPM, matched recording, correction map, or audio file has
+been verified for either. Import an actual local recording after running StemLab,
+or explicitly bake a chosen DanceRudiments catalogue pattern with the included
+native-only offline utility. Do not relabel synthetic preview as genuine audio
+analysis.
+
+See [`docs/09-song-reactive-showcase.md`](../../docs/09-song-reactive-showcase.md)
+for matching/export commands, provenance requirements, GPU shader contract and
+acceptance tests. This markdown relative path refers to the unimported source
+package; the package documentation remains accessible at its repository URL.
